## Heartbeat protocol (MEMORY_PROTOCOL §4.4 reference)

**When to heartbeat:**
- Every ~30 min of active work
- Before any `/compact` invocation
- Before laptop lid close / long pause
- When switching to a meaningfully different task

**What to include:**
- Current task name + sub-step
- File(s) being modified with line numbers
- Specific blocker if any
- Updated timestamp

**Compaction safety (§15):**
After compaction, the next session reads this heartbeat FIRST. Be SPECIFIC — vague heartbeats are useless after context loss. Say exactly what file, function, line, issue.

